<section class="cx-sec" id="calculators" aria-labelledby="calc">
  <h2 id="calc" class="cx-h2">Free SIP, Lumpsum and Investment Calculators for NISM Exams</h2>
  <p class="cx-calc-sub">Use our free SIP calculator, lumpsum calculator, Rule of 72 calculator and goal-based SIP calculator to practise the time value of money formulas tested in NISM Series V-A, X-A and XVII.</p>
  <div class="cx-calc" id="cxCalc">
    <div class="cx-ctabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Calculators">
      <button type="button" role="tab" id="ct-sip" aria-controls="cp-sip" aria-selected="true">SIP Future Value</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" id="ct-lump" aria-controls="cp-lump" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Lumpsum Growth</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" id="ct-r72" aria-controls="cp-r72" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Rule of 72</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" id="ct-goal" aria-controls="cp-goal" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Goal-based SIP</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-cpanel" role="tabpanel" id="cp-sip" aria-labelledby="ct-sip">
      <h3 class="cx-ch">SIP Calculator: Future Value of a Monthly SIP</h3>
      <p class="cx-clead">Find what a monthly Systematic Investment Plan (SIP) can grow to.</p>
      <div class="cx-cgrid"><label for="sipP">Monthly SIP (₹)<input id="sipP" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="5000" min="100" max="10000000" step="100" /></label><label for="sipR">Expected return (% per year)<input id="sipR" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="12" min="1" max="30" step="0.1" /></label><label for="sipN">Period (years)<input id="sipN" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="10" min="1" max="40" step="1" /></label></div>
      <div class="cx-cres" aria-live="polite"><p>Amount invested<b id="sipI">–</b></p><p>Estimated returns<b id="sipG">–</b></p><p>Total value<b id="sipV">–</b></p></div>
      <p class="cx-cform">Formula: FV = P × [(1 + i)<sup>n</sup> − 1] ÷ i × (1 + i), where P is the monthly SIP, i is the monthly return (annual return ÷ 12) and n is the number of months. Instalments are assumed at the start of each month.</p>
      <p class="cx-cnote">Used in NISM Series V-A and X-A. <a href="/nism-exams-5a-mutual-fund-distributors-certification-mock-tests">Try the V-A mock test</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-cpanel" role="tabpanel" id="cp-lump" aria-labelledby="ct-lump" hidden>
      <h3 class="cx-ch">Lumpsum Calculator: Growth of a One-Time Investment</h3>
      <p class="cx-clead">Find what a single investment can grow to with annual compounding.</p>
      <div class="cx-cgrid"><label for="lsP">One-time investment (₹)<input id="lsP" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="100000" min="1000" max="100000000" step="1000" /></label><label for="lsR">Expected return (% per year)<input id="lsR" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="10" min="1" max="30" step="0.1" /></label><label for="lsN">Period (years)<input id="lsN" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="10" min="1" max="40" step="1" /></label></div>
      <div class="cx-cres" aria-live="polite"><p>Amount invested<b id="lsI">–</b></p><p>Estimated returns<b id="lsG">–</b></p><p>Total value<b id="lsV">–</b></p></div>
      <p class="cx-cform">Formula: FV = P × (1 + r)<sup>t</sup>, where P is the amount invested, r is the annual return and t is the number of years.</p>
      <p class="cx-cnote">Used in NISM Series V-A and X-A. <a href="/nism-exams-10a-investment-adviser-level-1-certification-mock-tests">Try the X-A mock test</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-cpanel" role="tabpanel" id="cp-r72" aria-labelledby="ct-r72" hidden>
      <h3 class="cx-ch">Rule of 72 Calculator: Years to Double Your Money</h3>
      <p class="cx-clead">A quick estimate of how long money takes to double at a fixed return.</p>
      <div class="cx-cgrid"><label for="r72R">Return (% per year)<input id="r72R" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="8" min="0.5" max="50" step="0.1" /></label></div>
      <div class="cx-cres" aria-live="polite"><p>Years to double (Rule of 72)<b id="r72Y">–</b></p><p>Exact years to double<b id="r72E">–</b></p><p>Money after that time<b id="r72M">–</b></p></div>
      <p class="cx-cform">Formula: Years to double ≈ 72 ÷ annual return (%). The exact answer is ln(2) ÷ ln(1 + r), shown alongside for comparison.</p>
      <p class="cx-cnote">Used in NISM Series V-A and X-A. <a href="/nism-exams-5a-mutual-fund-distributors-certification-mock-tests">Try the V-A mock test</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-cpanel" role="tabpanel" id="cp-goal" aria-labelledby="ct-goal" hidden>
      <h3 class="cx-ch">Goal-Based SIP Calculator: Monthly SIP Needed for a Target</h3>
      <p class="cx-clead">Find the monthly SIP needed to reach a financial goal by a set date.</p>
      <div class="cx-cgrid"><label for="gsF">Goal amount (₹)<input id="gsF" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="1000000" min="10000" max="1000000000" step="10000" /></label><label for="gsR">Expected return (% per year)<input id="gsR" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="12" min="1" max="30" step="0.1" /></label><label for="gsN">Period (years)<input id="gsN" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="10" min="1" max="40" step="1" /></label></div>
      <div class="cx-cres" aria-live="polite"><p>Monthly SIP needed<b id="gsP">–</b></p><p>Amount invested<b id="gsI">–</b></p><p>Estimated returns<b id="gsG">–</b></p></div>
      <p class="cx-cform">Formula: P = FV × i ÷ {[(1 + i)<sup>n</sup> − 1] × (1 + i)}, where FV is the goal amount, i is the monthly return and n is the number of months.</p>
      <p class="cx-cnote">Used in NISM Series V-A, X-A and XVII. <a href="/nism-exams-10a-investment-adviser-level-1-certification-mock-tests">Try the X-A mock test</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="cx-cdisc">For learning only. Results are estimates, not investment advice.</p>
</section>
<script>
(function () {
  var box = document.getElementById('cxCalc'); if (!box) return;
  var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };
  var num = function (id) { var v = parseFloat($(id).value); return isFinite(v) && v > 0 ? v : 0; };
  var inr = function (v) { return isFinite(v) && v > 0 ? '₹' + Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-IN') : '–'; };
  var set = function (id, t) { $(id).textContent = t; };
  function calc() {
    var p = num('sipP'), i = num('sipR') / 1200, n = num('sipN') * 12;
    var fv = (p && i && n) ? p * ((Math.pow(1 + i, n) - 1) / i) * (1 + i) : 0;
    set('sipI', inr(p * n)); set('sipV', inr(fv)); set('sipG', inr(fv - p * n));
    var lp = num('lsP'), lr = num('lsR') / 100, ln = num('lsN');
    var lv = lp * Math.pow(1 + lr, ln);
    set('lsI', inr(lp)); set('lsV', inr(lv)); set('lsG', inr(lv - lp));
    var r = num('r72R');
    set('r72Y', r ? (72 / r).toFixed(1) + ' years' : '–');
    set('r72E', r ? (Math.log(2) / Math.log(1 + r / 100)).toFixed(1) + ' years' : '–');
    set('r72M', r ? 'About 2× your money' : '–');
    var f = num('gsF'), gi = num('gsR') / 1200, gn = num('gsN') * 12;
    var gp = (f && gi && gn) ? f * gi / ((Math.pow(1 + gi, gn) - 1) * (1 + gi)) : 0;
    set('gsP', inr(gp)); set('gsI', inr(gp * gn)); set('gsG', inr(f - gp * gn));
  }
  box.addEventListener('input', calc);
  box.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) { if (e.key === 'Enter' && e.target.tagName === 'INPUT') e.preventDefault(); });
  var tabs = [].slice.call(box.querySelectorAll('[role="tab"]'));
  function show(t) {
    tabs.forEach(function (x) { var on = x === t; x.setAttribute('aria-selected', on); x.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1; $(x.getAttribute('aria-controls')).hidden = !on; });
  }
  tabs.forEach(function (t, k) {
    t.addEventListener('click', function () { show(t); });
    t.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
      var d = e.key === 'ArrowRight' ? 1 : e.key === 'ArrowLeft' ? -1 : 0;
      if (d) { e.preventDefault(); var n = tabs[(k + d + tabs.length) % tabs.length]; show(n); n.focus(); }
    });
  });
  calc();
})();
</script>

<section class="cx-sec" aria-labelledby="faq">
  <h2 id="faq" class="cx-h2">Frequently Asked Questions About NISM Exams and Demo Test</h2>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>What is a NISM mock test?</h3></summary><div><p>A NISM mock test is a simulated practice exam of multiple-choice questions (MCQs) designed to mirror the format, difficulty and syllabus weightage of the official National Institute of Securities Markets certification exam.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>Can I try a free NISM demo test before buying a premium plan?</h3></summary><div><p>Yes. Open any course page on our platform and click ‘Start Free Demo’. Registration is required before the demo starts. The demo lets you try the test interface and judge the quality of our questions before you buy.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>Do your practice tests simulate the actual NISM exam format?</h3></summary><div><p>Yes. Every NISM practice test on our platform is designed to replicate the official testing environment, with a countdown timer as per the module’s official duration (typically 2 to 3 hours), a question navigation palette, and series-specific negative marking wherever the official exam applies it.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>Are the questions based on the latest 2026 syllabus?</h3></summary><div><p>Yes. Our content team of Chartered Accountants and NISM-certified professionals regularly reviews and updates the question banks in line with the latest 2026 NISM workbooks, SEBI circulars and Union Budget tax changes.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>What is the difference between a chapter-wise practice test and a full model test?</h3></summary><div><p>Chapter-wise practice tests let you focus on one topic, such as taxation or option Greeks, right after reading the study material. A full NISM model test follows the official question count and pattern of that module to test your overall readiness under real exam conditions.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>Will I get detailed explanations for incorrect answers?</h3></summary><div><p>Yes. Every question in our premium NISM mock test packages comes with a step-by-step explanation. For calculation-heavy modules such as Equity Derivatives and Research Analyst, we show the full working to build concept clarity.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>How long do I get access to the study materials?</h3></summary><div><p>You can choose a 15-day premium plan (from ₹599) for intensive last-minute revision, or a 30-day plan (from ₹699) for deeper study. Both give 24/7 access on desktop and mobile. Prices include taxes.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>Which NISM certification is best for beginners?</h3></summary><div><p>For people new to financial markets, NISM Series V-A: Mutual Fund Distributors is the usual starting point. It covers foundational concepts in investment planning and investor services, and has no negative marking.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>Is NISM certification mandatory to sell mutual funds?</h3></summary><div><p>Yes. Under SEBI regulations, passing the NISM Series V-A exam is mandatory for anyone who wants to work as a mutual fund distributor in India. After passing, you must also obtain an ARN from AMFI.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>What is the eligibility to take a NISM certification exam?</h3></summary><div><p>Most NISM exams have no minimum educational qualification and no upper age limit. Anyone interested in financial markets with a valid PAN and a government-issued photo ID can register and take the exam.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>How do I register for the official NISM exam online?</h3></summary><div><p>Register on the NISM Certification Portal, linked from the official NISM website (nism.ac.in). Create an account, upload your PAN and a valid government-issued ID, and wait for NISM to approve your registration. You can then choose your module, test centre and time slot, and pay the official exam fee.</p></div></details>
<details class="cx-faq"><summary><h3>Am I allowed to use a calculator during the NISM exam?</h3></summary><div><p>In centre-based NISM exams, a calculator is allowed if it is silent and has no computer connectivity. Mobile phones, smartwatches and tablets are not allowed. In NISM remote proctored exams, a physical calculator is not allowed; an on-screen scientific calculator is provided. Always check NISM’s latest candidate instructions before your exam.</p></div></details>
  <p class="cx-center"><a class="cx-btn cx-know" href="/nism-exams-mock-test-faqs">See All FAQs</a></p>
</section>

